WEBVTT

00:04.330 --> 00:07.860
A shoemaker living in Enberch 
died after eating some bread.

00:08.260 --> 00:11.490
The wheat that was used to 
make that bread was from this village.

00:15.930 --> 00:17.930
Ridelius' Hellfire...

00:17.930 --> 00:19.890
Ride... what now?

00:19.890 --> 00:22.040
It's wheat that's been poisoned by disease.

00:22.040 --> 00:25.790
You can't tell if it's poisoned a wheat field 
until someone dies from eating it.

00:27.360 --> 00:30.060
An official representative will be coming soon.

00:30.060 --> 00:33.240
Enberch plans to return 
all of the wheat from our village.

00:33.240 --> 00:36.050
R-Return all the wheat? That means...

00:36.050 --> 00:39.070
That's right. We have to return the money.

00:39.780 --> 00:41.680
Village Head, what should we do?

00:41.680 --> 00:43.260
We've already used the money

00:43.260 --> 00:45.740
to buy pigs and chickens, 
as well as mend our sickles and spades!

00:45.740 --> 00:47.280
That's not all.

00:47.650 --> 00:50.450
We had a bumper harvest this year.

00:50.450 --> 00:54.050
The quality of food and alcohol 
went up at my place.

00:54.050 --> 00:56.590
Your money's been spent there, too.

00:57.410 --> 00:58.820
And there's another problem...

00:58.820 --> 01:03.130
The scary thing about this is that it 
doesn't end with just a few deaths.

01:03.550 --> 01:06.360
There's no telling if other stalks 
have snuck their way in,

01:06.360 --> 01:10.210
so the entire harvest can no longer be eaten.

01:10.500 --> 01:13.210
We have no stores of wheat in the village.

01:13.210 --> 01:14.260
What are we going to do?!

01:14.260 --> 01:16.960
We can bear being poor, but we can't starve!

01:16.960 --> 01:19.390
Exactly, however...

01:19.870 --> 01:22.080
These two mixed poisonous 
wheat into our harvest!

01:22.080 --> 01:24.080
I heard they brought wheat to this village!

01:24.080 --> 01:24.880
That's right!

01:24.880 --> 01:27.360
Didn't you go to the waterwheel 
and grind your wheat into flour?!

01:27.360 --> 01:30.280
You conspired with the miller 
boy to destroy this village!

01:30.280 --> 01:32.280
That's right! Where'd that liar go?!

01:32.280 --> 01:35.820
Tie them both up and make them confess 
which batches of wheat they poisoned!

01:35.820 --> 01:37.020
Please hold on!

01:37.020 --> 01:39.300
Stay out of this, woman!

01:39.300 --> 01:40.480
Excuse me?

01:42.250 --> 01:43.990
Evan is in the church.

01:44.300 --> 01:46.020
What matters most right now

01:46.020 --> 01:50.650
is that the wheat will be returned
 and how we can pay them back.

01:50.650 --> 01:53.090
We can't pay back money we don't have.

01:53.090 --> 01:55.280
We'll have to ask them 
to wait until next year...

01:55.280 --> 01:57.020
I hope things will be that simple.

01:57.020 --> 01:58.010
What do you mean?

01:58.360 --> 02:03.100
Enberch might use this as an excuse to 
change our relationship back to how it was...

02:03.100 --> 02:04.500
Wh-What are you saying?!

02:04.500 --> 02:06.650
Those guys shouldn't be able 
to lay their hands on us.

02:06.650 --> 02:08.790
Didn't Father Franz set it up that way?

02:09.190 --> 02:11.790
It was impossible for Elsa from the start!

02:11.790 --> 02:13.630
Of course they'd look down on her!

02:13.630 --> 02:17.650
That's right! She stays in the church all day 
and never comes out to help in the fields!

02:17.650 --> 02:20.780
The wheat harvest this year 
was all thanks to Lord Truyeo!

02:20.780 --> 02:22.980
A church girl like her is completely useless!

02:22.980 --> 02:23.870
That's enough.

02:24.770 --> 02:28.090
Every villager needs to check how much money 
they have left after selling the harvest

02:28.090 --> 02:30.880
and how many provisions 
they already have prepared.

02:30.880 --> 02:34.440
At the earliest, the messenger 
will reach our village by daybreak.

02:34.440 --> 02:36.590
Let's disperse for now.

02:43.850 --> 02:45.100
Elsa.

02:45.100 --> 02:47.640
I'm sure this is painful for you, 
but please endure it for now.

02:49.480 --> 02:52.220
Ms. Iima, please go to the church with Elsa.

02:52.220 --> 02:55.330
Some of the hot-blooded villagers 
may come pounding on the door.

02:55.330 --> 02:56.280
Leave it to me.

02:56.980 --> 03:02.200
Mr. Lawrence, I'm just as suspicious 
of you as the villagers are.

03:02.200 --> 03:06.910
Even so, please don't think that I'm foolish 
enough to immediately believe that as truth.

03:06.910 --> 03:10.460
I would say the exact same thing 
if I were in your place, Village Head Sem.

03:10.820 --> 03:16.240
In order to ensure your safety 
and prevent further suspicion,

03:16.240 --> 03:18.510
I'd like the two of you to come to my home.

03:31.100 --> 03:38.820
Spice and Wolf

04:51.970 --> 04:55.980
<b>Episode 23
Orchestrated Catastrophe
and Appropriate Retribution</b>

04:54.350 --> 04:57.060
The situation seems to be 
too much of a coincidence.

04:57.060 --> 05:00.500
The more I think about it, the more 
I feel like Enberch orchestrated all of this

05:00.500 --> 05:02.170
in order to control Tereo.

05:02.170 --> 05:03.650
I agree.

05:03.650 --> 05:08.320
Even so, Elsa's backer wouldn't stay 
silent if the village gets trapped like that.

05:08.320 --> 05:11.500
That's why they needed a scapegoat.

05:11.500 --> 05:14.080
Then we happened by,
 giving them the perfect opportunity.

05:14.620 --> 05:17.240
They'll surely offer the village this deal.

05:17.730 --> 05:22.610
"We'll delay the return payment for 
the wheat if you hand over the culprits to us."

05:22.610 --> 05:24.840
Are you going to allow that?

05:24.840 --> 05:25.980
Of course not.

05:25.980 --> 05:26.910
However...

05:27.800 --> 05:30.770
Yes. If we run, it would be like 
admitting we poisoned the wheat.

05:30.770 --> 05:32.640
Your image would be posted everywhere and...

05:32.920 --> 05:36.000
My life as a merchant would be over.

05:38.060 --> 05:41.630
Could we seek help 
from that association of yours?

05:41.630 --> 05:44.590
The association, huh? If only...

05:45.100 --> 05:46.610
Oh, that's right.

05:49.390 --> 05:51.140
If I rode on your back,

05:51.140 --> 05:53.440
we could flee to another
 town faster than on horseback.

05:53.440 --> 05:54.670
Of course.

05:54.670 --> 05:58.370
It would be a huge problem if news got out 
that a merchant poisoned some wheat.

05:58.370 --> 06:00.750
The association would 
fervently deny such accusations.

06:00.750 --> 06:06.240
If that is the case, the ones 
trying to entrap us may give up.

06:06.240 --> 06:09.390
But then, who would take the blame instead?

06:09.950 --> 06:12.530
They'd blame Evan, since he could
 poison the wheat at any time

06:12.530 --> 06:15.060
and the villagers have 
always been suspicious of him.

06:15.520 --> 06:17.680
Then, I shall carry him on my back as well.

06:17.960 --> 06:19.400
But then...

06:19.400 --> 06:22.310
If that girl is in danger, 
I shall carry her as well.

06:22.620 --> 06:25.420
You are foolishly good-natured, after all.

06:25.420 --> 06:26.940
Goodness, how troublesome...

06:27.280 --> 06:29.150
I'm sorry. Thank you.

06:29.890 --> 06:30.660
Well, then.

06:31.070 --> 06:34.030
Please tell me who in the world 
the two of you are.

06:34.340 --> 06:36.740
I have already told you.

06:36.740 --> 06:39.200
Yes, you have.

06:39.200 --> 06:40.820
And you probably speak the truth.

06:41.250 --> 06:47.210
However, the two of you were seeking 
Diendran Abbey. For what reason?

06:47.210 --> 06:51.300
A person I met in Kumerson 
introduced me to the abbot of that abbey.

06:51.610 --> 06:55.810
So, you didn't come here at 
the request of the town of Enberch?

06:56.130 --> 07:00.490
It's true that we stopped by the town 
of Enberch, but we only passed through.

07:00.490 --> 07:05.900
We came in search of Diendran Abbey 
only for our own selves.

07:05.900 --> 07:08.080
Y-You're lying!

07:09.580 --> 07:14.160
We have absolutely nothing to do with 
the feud between Enberch and this village.

07:14.160 --> 07:18.480
I only found out about the feud 
after coming to this village

07:18.480 --> 07:21.020
and I used my own experience 
to deduce the situation.

07:21.020 --> 07:24.880
You absolutely, truly, 
have nothing to do with any of this?

07:24.880 --> 07:25.840
Yes.

07:25.840 --> 07:28.050
If that's truly the case...

07:28.050 --> 07:32.630
If that's truly the case, can you lend us 
some wisdom and perhaps some money?

07:32.630 --> 07:34.850
I can lend you my wisdom, however...

07:35.160 --> 07:36.990
I won't ask you to lend it to us 
free of charge.

07:37.620 --> 07:40.520
In exchange, I can guarantee your safety.

07:40.930 --> 07:42.310
Is that a threat?

07:42.310 --> 07:45.120
The only reason I did not simply 
tie you up as the culprit was

07:45.120 --> 07:48.980
because you brought wheat as a gift 
when you came to greet me.

07:50.370 --> 07:53.490
It looks like I have no choice but to agree.

07:54.740 --> 07:55.580
However.

07:55.950 --> 08:00.580
I will ask for appropriate compensation 
if I'm able to turn this situation around.

08:01.830 --> 08:03.640
I understand.

08:04.890 --> 08:07.400
Then, let me say this first.

08:07.400 --> 08:10.400
This commotion was all orchestrated 
by the town of Enberch itself.

08:11.060 --> 08:12.060
Please continue.

08:12.060 --> 08:12.720
Yes.

08:13.100 --> 08:15.770
This is what I expect Enberch's plan to be.

08:15.770 --> 08:19.570
You will not be able to pay back 
the money for all the wheat.

08:19.570 --> 08:24.940
So, they will demand you credit them 
towards the wheat you harvest next year.

08:25.250 --> 08:26.520
What does that mean?

08:26.520 --> 08:31.710
They will negotiate the price of next year's 
wheat and buy it at that price now.

08:31.710 --> 08:35.470
However, since they're buying 
something that doesn't exist yet,

08:35.470 --> 08:36.950
they'll haggle down the price.

08:38.430 --> 08:42.770
You'll be forced to make up the difference
 with the following year's wheat.

08:42.770 --> 08:45.810
Repeating this cycle will become
 increasingly difficult for your village.

08:45.810 --> 08:48.770
In the end, they will probably 
take advantage of your weakness

08:48.770 --> 08:52.300
to end the contract made with Father Franz.

08:53.730 --> 08:56.410
We only wished to avoid 
heavy taxation in our village.

08:56.410 --> 09:01.630
Thinking that, we desperately 
protected what Father Franz left us.

09:01.630 --> 09:04.140
I can't believe they used 
Ridelius' Hellfire against us...

09:04.140 --> 09:09.490
Is there really no chance the poisonous
 wheat made it into your harvest?

09:09.490 --> 09:13.370
That cursed wheat is black and sticky.

09:13.370 --> 09:15.560
Everyone in the village can recognize it.

09:15.560 --> 09:20.200
It's unlikely that enough to kill someone
 was carelessly mixed into our harvest.

09:22.920 --> 09:29.080
I spoke with Elsa a bit, and she 
immediately suspected Enberch.

09:30.490 --> 09:32.360
I am so pathetic.

09:32.360 --> 09:35.850
I thought our livelihood would be secure 
as long as we had someone to buy our wheat,

09:35.850 --> 09:38.890
so I didn't consider anything else.

09:39.390 --> 09:42.600
I can't believe they'd 
attack us in such a way...

09:42.600 --> 09:46.100
I'd like to speak with Ms. Elsa.

09:53.230 --> 09:54.740
You want to meet with Elsa?

09:54.740 --> 10:00.490
Village Head Sem has promised our safety 
in exchange for my wisdom and money.

10:00.490 --> 10:04.830
I need to speak with Miss Elsa 
to gain some accurate information.

10:05.380 --> 10:07.080
Elsa! Elsa!

10:08.970 --> 10:10.000
What is it?

10:10.000 --> 10:12.110
I've come to talk with you.

10:12.810 --> 10:13.800
You all right?

10:14.340 --> 10:17.910
We cannot depend on them, 
but we can trust them.

10:17.910 --> 10:22.210
At the very least, the two of them 
know the proper method of prayer.

10:22.210 --> 10:23.220
Got it.

10:26.420 --> 10:27.400
Please come in.

10:29.000 --> 10:30.090
Please stay outside.

10:30.090 --> 10:31.360
Wh-Why?

10:31.360 --> 10:32.520
Please.

10:33.550 --> 10:34.820
Fine...

10:34.820 --> 10:35.560
Evan.

10:37.940 --> 10:41.570
Any merchant would cry
 if they dropped this purse.

10:42.680 --> 10:44.880
Think of it as proof that you can trust me.

10:52.410 --> 10:55.030
I can't believe Enberch 
would use such underhanded tricks...

10:55.940 --> 11:00.620
My backer is merely supporting me 
because of my father.

11:00.620 --> 11:03.850
If I ask for much more, 
I risk losing my backer completely...

11:03.850 --> 11:05.490
As expected...

11:05.490 --> 11:09.810
So, what do you think will happen 
to us after this, Ms. Elsa?

11:10.100 --> 11:11.730
You're asking me?

11:11.730 --> 11:14.510
I think only you, and perhaps Ms. Iima,

11:14.510 --> 11:17.720
are able to tell how Enberch 
plans to play this out.

11:17.720 --> 11:19.940
As well as the two of you, right?

11:24.040 --> 11:26.280
We are thinking of running.

11:26.280 --> 11:31.040
I cannot believe you'd be able to escape, 
even with a horse.

11:31.040 --> 11:34.540
That would be the case if my companion 
was a mere girl like she seems.

11:38.420 --> 11:40.880
Then, why haven't you fled?

11:41.250 --> 11:45.820
First, we haven't finished reading 
through the books in this church.

11:45.820 --> 11:51.140
The next reason is that we know 
who will be blamed if we disappear.

11:53.110 --> 11:55.940
Are you confident 
you'll be able to escape with Evan?

11:55.940 --> 11:58.020
Not just him, but you as well.

12:00.280 --> 12:03.580
There is no reason for me to refuse 
your request to read the books.

12:03.580 --> 12:04.950
But there isn't much time...

12:04.950 --> 12:07.790
There is only one book 
we'd like to read, no matter what.

12:09.020 --> 12:11.420
It has been hidden under the altar.

12:11.420 --> 12:13.150
As long as I can read that book...

12:13.660 --> 12:16.460
Well, considering the current 
predicament, I will not wish for more.

12:24.850 --> 12:26.320
Goodness.

12:26.820 --> 12:30.070
There should be a book 
under the alter. Go get it.

12:31.230 --> 12:32.950
Y-Yeah.

12:34.680 --> 12:37.950
I will neither encourage 
nor discourage you from escaping.

12:37.950 --> 12:42.150
However, will you lend me your 
merchant's wisdom until that time?

12:43.260 --> 12:46.490
I'm not sure if I can 
give you a satisfactory answer.

12:46.490 --> 12:49.830
It seems merchants really like that phrase.

12:49.830 --> 12:51.840
We are a cautious lot.

12:52.870 --> 12:54.400
I brought the book.

12:54.400 --> 12:55.750
But this...

12:56.090 --> 12:58.540
Isn't this one of Father Franz's 
books on pagan legends?

12:58.540 --> 12:59.590
Whoa!

13:01.150 --> 13:02.800
Ms. Elsa, please excuse me.

13:11.410 --> 13:12.640
Hey.

13:12.640 --> 13:17.360
If I tear this book apart in anger, 
will you apologize on my behalf?

13:17.360 --> 13:21.400
I don't mind apologizing, but don't tear 
the book apart just to wipe your tears.

13:22.810 --> 13:27.150
You would happily buy my tears at a high price.

13:27.150 --> 13:29.370
It would be a waste not to cry before you.

13:29.370 --> 13:32.240
Such expensive gems, 
I'll have to make sure they're not fake.

13:36.620 --> 13:38.850
I would like to read alone.

13:38.850 --> 13:40.530
Tell me your thoughts after you finish.

13:40.530 --> 13:41.340
Yes...

13:46.760 --> 13:47.420
Oh.

13:57.460 --> 13:59.730
I'll be by your side no matter what happens...

13:59.730 --> 14:02.070
There's no need for you to worry, Elsa!

14:02.070 --> 14:02.760
Yeah...

14:08.450 --> 14:11.030
If I shouldn't be here, I'll step out.

14:12.010 --> 14:16.290
So, what can my knowledge 
and experience help you with?

14:17.460 --> 14:19.340
According to Village Head Sem,

14:19.340 --> 14:22.880
we'll be seventy Rimmer coins short 
if they return all the wheat to us.

14:22.880 --> 14:25.460
Seventy Rimmer. That's a lot.

14:25.780 --> 14:28.300
That's not all.

14:28.300 --> 14:33.210
Since the wheat we stored can no longer 
be used, we'll also need money for food...

14:33.890 --> 14:38.140
I thought things wouldn't come to this 
as long as we still had father's contract.

14:38.430 --> 14:40.680
That way of thinking isn't wrong.

14:40.680 --> 14:45.280
However, the villagers never understood 
the greatness of that blessing.

14:45.630 --> 14:50.010
I heard from my father that 
farmers in other villages work hard

14:50.010 --> 14:52.590
doing odd jobs throughout the winter.

14:52.590 --> 14:57.120
They try to earn as much money as possible, 
so their land isn't taken from them.

14:57.120 --> 14:58.040
But here...

14:58.040 --> 15:02.210
That's right. However, 
nothing will change if we just grieve.

15:02.210 --> 15:04.270
Yes, you're right.

15:04.270 --> 15:08.260
If I merely grieve, my father... 
Father Franz will get angry with me...

15:09.990 --> 15:10.680
Ms. Elsa!

15:10.960 --> 15:13.120
Elsa! Elsa!

15:11.420 --> 15:12.380
Ms. Elsa!

15:20.030 --> 15:21.350
Hey, Mr. Lawrence.

15:21.720 --> 15:24.990
Everyone in the village 
suspects the two of us, don't they?

15:24.990 --> 15:25.970
That's right.

15:25.970 --> 15:27.110
Of course they do...

15:27.470 --> 15:32.120
I eavesdropped, but... you said you can escape?

15:32.120 --> 15:33.530
That?

15:33.530 --> 15:35.290
Yeah, we can.

15:35.290 --> 15:38.760
I'd like to selfishly 
take the two of you with me, too.

15:38.760 --> 15:40.720
That's not selfish at all.

15:40.720 --> 15:42.780
I don't want to die 
in a place like this. Elsa, too.

15:42.780 --> 15:45.130
I'm sure she wants to leave this village, too.

15:45.130 --> 15:47.780
Everyone says Mr. Franz is their benefactor,

15:47.780 --> 15:49.860
but no one in the village 
really appreciates it...

15:52.450 --> 15:55.220
They never listen to his teachings.

15:55.220 --> 15:58.190
They've always given 
their god a ton of offerings

15:58.190 --> 16:00.940
but have never offered a single 
piece of bread to the church.

16:00.940 --> 16:05.300
Without the village head or Ms. Iima, we 
would have starved to death a long time ago.

16:05.300 --> 16:08.070
It's true that the outside world isn't easy,

16:08.070 --> 16:10.210
but it might be easier than this village.

16:10.210 --> 16:11.360
Ms. Iima...

16:11.360 --> 16:12.990
You're, um...

16:12.990 --> 16:14.580
My name is Lawrence.

16:14.580 --> 16:19.870
Mr. Lawrence, if you want to escape 
with the two of them, I think you should.

16:21.080 --> 16:23.120
No, I hope you do.

16:23.120 --> 16:23.980
Yeah.

16:24.430 --> 16:27.430
Then, I'll need to convince Elsa.

16:31.650 --> 16:36.260
I know what I said, but how do 
you all plan on escaping?

16:36.260 --> 16:41.460
If a man can come across a maiden
 brewing beer in the mountains,

16:41.460 --> 16:45.770
it wouldn't be odd for another man 
to encounter something else equally strange.

16:47.090 --> 16:49.230
Did you meet a fairy or something?

16:49.230 --> 16:50.750
Something like that.

16:59.800 --> 17:01.810
Have you finished talking?

17:01.810 --> 17:02.820
More or less.

17:03.250 --> 17:05.940
I have already accomplished my goal.

17:05.940 --> 17:06.990
I see.

17:08.280 --> 17:10.600
If you are curious, you should read it as well.

17:10.600 --> 17:11.400
Yeah.

17:15.500 --> 17:18.300
"The gods of the land all fled in terror."

17:18.300 --> 17:20.940
"In the time it took for nuts 
of a tree to fall,

17:20.940 --> 17:24.060
Yoitsu was shredded apart by the bear's claws."

17:25.020 --> 17:26.020
That's all there is?

17:32.030 --> 17:37.620
I sense an infuriating gaze on me. 
Is it my imagination?

17:37.620 --> 17:38.660
I'm not...

17:39.990 --> 17:42.850
No, I am. You're right. I'm sorry.

17:42.850 --> 17:44.120
Don't get so angry.

17:45.330 --> 17:49.770
I am satisfied to hear that my old 
friends seemed to have gotten away.

17:49.770 --> 17:51.930
There was nothing else.

17:51.930 --> 17:55.070
Nothing in the world ever goes as one wishes.

17:55.070 --> 17:56.420
I cannot agree more.

17:56.740 --> 17:58.970
So, what are we going to do?

17:58.970 --> 18:01.640
We should escape quickly,
 if we plan to do so.

18:01.640 --> 18:03.100
Of course, we'll escape.

18:05.390 --> 18:07.870
You are taking a great loss this time.

18:07.870 --> 18:08.990
It can't be helped.

18:08.990 --> 18:11.200
We can't take the wheat with us.

18:11.530 --> 18:16.100
If the goods were expensive and
 more portable, we'd have options.

18:16.100 --> 18:18.800
Are you speaking of the pepper 
you sold once before?

18:18.800 --> 18:23.700
There is something more valuable 
and easier to carry than spices.

18:23.700 --> 18:24.450
Oh?

18:25.100 --> 18:26.080
Trust.

18:26.080 --> 18:29.830
It seems I will have to sell your trust 
once it grows higher in value.

18:29.830 --> 18:34.300
Do you know how paranoid of you I've 
become now that you've teased me so much?

18:36.780 --> 18:39.150
Then, I'll just have to regain that trust.

18:39.780 --> 18:42.460
This is the very reason 
I'm always suspicious of you!

18:42.460 --> 18:44.730
Lies will only lower the value of your trust.

18:45.930 --> 18:49.320
Well, you have never once blamed me 
for the trouble we are in.

18:49.320 --> 18:50.940
I am honestly grateful for that.

18:51.340 --> 18:51.860
Huh?

18:52.250 --> 18:56.510
You would not have taken a loss 
if I had not wished to come here.

18:56.510 --> 19:00.600
Then, it looks like we'll have to tighten your 
food and drinking budget to make up for it.

19:00.600 --> 19:04.280
You have grown quite unrestrained lately.

19:05.800 --> 19:07.560
Hand over that merchant!

19:07.560 --> 19:09.250
This is definitely their fault!

19:09.250 --> 19:11.170
Hand over the miller, too!

19:17.470 --> 19:20.000
Don't come over. Go deeper inside.

19:20.000 --> 19:21.050
But...

19:21.050 --> 19:22.700
I'll go out and persuade them.

19:22.700 --> 19:24.160
Don't be stupid.

19:24.160 --> 19:25.040
But...

19:29.900 --> 19:32.520
You'll just add oil to the fire.

19:32.520 --> 19:35.620
You're close with Evan.

19:35.620 --> 19:39.930
They might hand you over to Enberch 
as a heretic to get on the town's good side.

19:40.470 --> 19:41.550
Listen to me.

19:41.550 --> 19:44.600
The two of you can't stay 
in this village any longer.

19:45.390 --> 19:47.150
If it's hard to make a living everywhere,

19:47.150 --> 19:51.270
but it's better to look for a new life 
out there with someone you trust.

19:53.070 --> 19:55.490
You might have to give up a lot of things,

19:55.490 --> 19:58.420
but there should be a lot 
of things you'll gain on the way.

19:58.980 --> 20:01.010
No matter the journey,

20:01.010 --> 20:03.130
choosing your path at a fork
 takes only an instant.

20:03.690 --> 20:05.070
I couldn't agree more.

20:11.620 --> 20:12.920
I'd like to run.

20:14.290 --> 20:15.100
Yeah.

20:19.830 --> 20:23.680
I have one condition,
if you'd like to leave it to me.

20:26.070 --> 20:30.790
Think of everything that happens 
after this as a dream before the dawn.

20:32.330 --> 20:37.040
I'm a fairy that brews beer, after all. 
I'm so drunk I won't remember a thing.

20:37.580 --> 20:39.780
Then, leave it all to me.

20:39.780 --> 20:40.460
Just...

20:40.770 --> 20:45.450
I can easily jump over the crowd 
with all of you on my back,

20:45.450 --> 20:48.090
but I am not sure if you can 
withstand such a thing.

20:48.090 --> 20:49.970
Is there a back door in this church?

20:51.880 --> 20:55.190
I heard from Father Franz that there was 
an underground passage in the basement...

20:55.470 --> 20:56.600
Let's use that.

20:56.940 --> 20:59.720
Ms. Elsa and Evan should prepare 
to leave immediately.

20:59.720 --> 21:01.260
Y-Yes.

21:01.260 --> 21:05.160
Well, it's lucky enough to be able to make 
some preparations for your escape.

21:05.160 --> 21:09.970
It is not as though your hometown will 
disappear tomorrow. Be glad it still exists.

21:09.970 --> 21:12.000
Oh? You, too, Ms. Fairy?

21:12.000 --> 21:15.620
Do not lump me together 
with such weak creatures.

21:16.790 --> 21:18.600
We will prepare immediately.

21:19.150 --> 21:21.710
All right, then. Off you go!

21:22.260 --> 21:25.800
Even I have lost to her 
strong sense of presence.

21:27.260 --> 21:28.900
Do not worry.

21:29.820 --> 21:32.620
This is the only human form I can take.

21:32.620 --> 21:33.850
That's unfortunate.

21:34.200 --> 21:37.480
I prefer a woman with a more ample figure.

21:39.820 --> 21:40.780
Ouch!

21:41.770 --> 21:44.400
Hurry up and open the door to the basement.

22:04.680 --> 22:06.300
Then, are you ready?

22:06.610 --> 22:08.220
Y-Yeah.

22:08.220 --> 22:08.930
Yes.

23:44.940 --> 23:49.940
Episode 24

23:44.940 --> 23:49.940
Path of the Snake God and Answer of the Wise Wolf

23:45.900 --> 23:49.120
